{
  "document_title": "Medicare Program; Inpatient Rehabilitation Facility Prospective Payment System for Federal Fiscal Year 2025 and Updates to the IRF Quality Reporting Program",
  "agency": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS), Department of Health and Human Services (HHS)",
  "publication_date": "March 29, 2024",
  "summary": "Proposes FY 2025 updates to the Inpatient Rehabilitation Facility (IRF) Prospective Payment System (PPS) and changes to the IRF Quality Reporting Program (QRP). Key proposals: update CMG relative weights and average length-of-stay values using FY 2023 claims and FY 2022 cost report data in a budget-neutral manner; apply a market basket update (projected 3.2%) reduced by a 0.4% productivity adjustment for a proposed 2.8% payment update; adopt revised OMB CBSA delineations from OMB Bulletin No. 23-01 for the FY 2025 wage index and apply a 3-year phase-out of the 14.9% rural adjustment for IRFs reclassified from rural to urban; continue wage-index methodologies including a permanent 5% cap on wage-index decreases; propose a FY 2025 labor-related share of 74.2% and budget-neutral wage and CMG adjustment factors resulting in a proposed standard payment conversion factor of $18,872; update the outlier threshold from $10,423 to $12,158 to target outlier payments at ~3% of total payments; propose updated national urban/rural cost-to-charge ratio (CCR) averages (0.406 urban, 0.492 rural) and a CCR ceiling of 1.52. For the IRF QRP, proposes adding four standardized patient assessment data elements (Living Situation, two Food items, Utilities), modifying Transportation, and removing Admission Class beginning with FY 2028 QRP; requests information on future quality measure concepts and an IRF star rating system. Comments due by May 28, 2024."
}

